        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Please note this is a blank canvas and there is no ESB or Water supply \r\n\r\nCharming Traditional Stone Cottage with Excellent Potential\r\nA unique opportunity to acquire a traditional stone-built cottage, stone cart house and new horse stables, all set on approximately ½ acre. Located close to H91 KXY4\r\nThis attractive property offers a wonderful opportunity for those looking to create a character-filled home in a peaceful rural setting. The traditional stone cottage retains its original character and, together with the stone-built cart house and new horse stables, provides an excellent range of buildings with considerable potential for renovation and further development, subject to the necessary planning permissions.\r\nThe cottage offers a blank canvas for the discerning purchaser to restore and transform into a charming countryside residence. The existing stone-built cart house adds further character and could offer a variety of potential uses, while the recently constructed horse stables will appeal to equestrian enthusiasts or those seeking useful additional outbuildings.\r\nThe property is situated on approximately ½ acre and benefits from public water available on the main road. Access is via a shared driveway.\r\nThis is a particularly interesting property for anyone seeking a traditional stone cottage with land, character and a range of existing outbuildings, offering scope to create something truly special.\r\nProperty Features\r\n•\tTraditional stone-built cottage\r\n•\tStone-built cart house\r\n•\tNew horse stables\r\n•\tApproximately ½ acre\r\n•\tPublic water available on the main road\r\n•\tShared driveway access\r\n•\tExcellent renovation potential\r\n•\tCharacter property with a range of traditional and modern outbuildings\r\n•\tIdeal for those seeking a rural project or equestrian property\r\n•\tDevelopment potential, subject to planning permission\r\n•\tEligible for the Derelict Property Grant & the SEAI Grant\r\n\r\nViewing is highly recommended to appreciate the character and potential this unique property has to offer.\r\nPlease arrange through Vincent Walsh Auctioneers, we remain ultra flexible around viewings.\r\nPLEASE NOTE VIEWINGS ARE STRICTLY PRIVATE BY APPOINTMENT ONLY IN THE COMPANY OF THE AUCTIONEER MR VINCENT WALSH.\r\n\r\nNOTE: These particulars are not to be considered a formal offer. They are for information only and give a general idea of the property. They are not to be taken as forming any part of a resulting contract, nor to be relied upon as statements or representations of fact. Whilst every care is taken in their preparation, neither Vincent Walsh Auctioneer nor the vendor accepts any liability as to their accuracy. Intending purchasers must satisfy themselves by personal inspection or otherwise as to the correctness of these particulars. No person in the employment of Vincent Walsh Auctioneer has any authority to make or give any representation or warranty whatever in relation to this property."
      },
